(A triple-blind sham-controlled design for evaluating non-invasive brain stimulation in) Tj
T*
(alcohol dependence) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Background: Limited pharmaceutical options exist for individuals with severe alcohol) Tj
T*
(dependence, creating need for novel interventions. Non-invasive neuromodulation techniques) Tj
T*
(may offer adjunctive benefit. This protocol describes a prospective, multi-site trial) Tj
T*
(examining whether direct current stimulation can reduce drinking behaviors in adults with) Tj
T*
(alcohol use disorder. Methods: We will recruit 350 adults with confirmed alcohol use) Tj
T*
(disorder from 14 clinical sites. Participants will be randomly assigned 1:1 to receive) Tj
T*
(either active stimulation \(electrodes positioned at F4/F3, 2 mA current\) delivered daily) Tj
T*
(for five consecutive days, or matched sham stimulation. Both groups will undergo follow-up) Tj
T*
(assessments every 4 weeks throughout the 24-week study period. Randomization will be) Tj
T*
(stratified by site and baseline consumption severity. Participants, assessors, and) Tj
T*
(clinicians will be blinded to treatment allocation. Primary outcomes will include drinking) Tj
T*
(frequency metrics and weekly alcohol volume. Eligibility: adults aged 30-70 with) Tj
T*
(documented alcohol use disorder, stable housing, capacity to provide informed consent.) Tj
T*
(Study design: triple-blind, parallel-group, randomized controlled trial.) Tj
ET
